\section{Discussion}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Qwen is the strongest model, especially in zero-shot English.
    \item LLaMA is flexible but output can be unstable.
    \item DeBERTa is reasonable for semantic matching but weaker on implicit causality.
\end{itemize}

\section{Next Steps}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Hybrid systems combining LLM scoring + encoder features
    \item RLHF-style feedback for better explanation ranking
    \item Ensemble multiple experts and retrieval-enhanced reasoning
\end{itemize}

\section{Conclusion}
Abductive reasoning is challenging with distractor documents. Qwen shows strong initial performance. Future work focuses on hybrid modeling, structured reasoning, and improved prompting.

